1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,839
Thirty-four minutes past six,

2
00:00:00,840 --> 00:00:03,220
on a Saturday evening in Seoul,

3
00:00:03,280 --> 00:00:05,679
someone pushed their way out of a crowded alley,

4
00:00:05,680 --> 00:00:08,092
took out a phone, and called the police.

5
00:00:08,152 --> 00:00:10,528
It was not a crime they were reporting.

6
00:00:10,588 --> 00:00:12,447
They said people were being forced uphill

7
00:00:12,448 --> 00:00:14,147
into a place where there was no room

8
00:00:14,148 --> 00:00:14,987
to come back down,

9
00:00:14,988 --> 00:00:17,933
and that somebody should come and control it.

10
00:00:17,993 --> 00:00:22,380
Ten more people were going to make that same call.

11
00:00:22,440 --> 00:00:24,259
This is a story about a street,

12
00:00:24,260 --> 00:00:26,674
a telephone number, and a definition.

13
00:00:26,734 --> 00:00:29,296
The street is about fifty metres long.

14
00:00:29,356 --> 00:00:32,150
At the top it is about five metres wide.

15
00:00:32,210 --> 00:00:34,586
At the bottom it is three point two.

16
00:00:34,646 --> 00:00:36,545
The telephone number is one-one-two,

17
00:00:36,546 --> 00:00:38,005
which in South Korea is what you dial

18
00:00:38,006 --> 00:00:39,251
for the police.

19
00:00:39,311 --> 00:00:40,870
And the definition is the one

20
00:00:40,871 --> 00:00:43,270
the country's disaster and safety law used

21
00:00:43,271 --> 00:00:44,511
for an event:

22
00:00:44,571 --> 00:00:46,251
something with an organiser,

23
00:00:46,311 --> 00:00:48,017
somebody whose name is on it,

24
00:00:48,071 --> 00:00:50,789
somebody who files a safety plan in advance.

25
00:00:50,849 --> 00:00:52,828
That definition is a real sentence

26
00:00:52,829 --> 00:00:54,828
in a real statute with a number on it,

27
00:00:54,829 --> 00:00:57,028
and by the end of this film you are going

28
00:00:57,029 --> 00:00:59,634
to hear the sentence that replaced it.

29
00:00:59,694 --> 00:01:01,213
On the night this film is about,

30
00:01:01,214 --> 00:01:03,993
an estimated hundred thousand people came

31
00:01:03,994 --> 00:01:06,353
to a district where nothing had an organiser

32
00:01:06,354 --> 00:01:07,411
at all.

33
00:01:07,471 --> 00:01:09,030
By the end of that night a hundred

34
00:01:09,031 --> 00:01:11,031
and fifty-nine people were dead,

35
00:01:11,091 --> 00:01:12,770
and by the end of the following year

36
00:01:12,771 --> 00:01:14,951
a court had convicted one official,

37
00:01:15,011 --> 00:01:16,251
acquitted another,

38
00:01:16,311 --> 00:01:18,450
and explained the difference in a single sentence

39
00:01:18,451 --> 00:01:20,714
about who the law was written for.

40
00:01:20,774 --> 00:01:22,813
Over the next half hour you will hear what eleven

41
00:01:22,814 --> 00:01:24,520
people said when they called,

42
00:01:24,574 --> 00:01:26,313
what the state did with four of those calls

43
00:01:26,314 --> 00:01:27,954
and did not do with seven,

44
00:01:28,014 --> 00:01:30,134
where its officers were instead,

45
00:01:30,194 --> 00:01:32,915
and why the district office walked out of court.

46
00:01:32,916 --> 00:01:35,199
The question is not who to blame.

47
00:01:35,259 --> 00:01:36,718
It is what happens to a warning

48
00:01:36,719 --> 00:01:40,064
after somebody makes it.

49
00:01:40,124 --> 00:01:41,183
Start with the street,

50
00:01:41,184 --> 00:01:42,663
because the street is the part

51
00:01:42,664 --> 00:01:44,962
of this that anyone can stand in.

52
00:01:45,022 --> 00:01:46,662
It runs off Itaewon-ro,

53
00:01:46,722 --> 00:01:50,161
the main road through the district,
up between the back of the Hamilton Hotel

54
00:01:50,162 --> 00:01:51,809
and the buildings behind it,

55
00:01:51,862 --> 00:01:53,435
toward the streets above.

56
00:01:53,495 --> 00:01:55,894
Exit One of Itaewon station comes up almost

57
00:01:55,895 --> 00:01:57,218
at the foot of it.

58
00:01:57,278 --> 00:01:59,437
If you have been to any city in the world,

59
00:01:59,438 --> 00:02:02,301
you have walked up a street like this one.

60
00:02:02,361 --> 00:02:03,808
It is a shortcut.

61
00:02:03,868 --> 00:02:05,667
It is how people get from the station

62
00:02:05,668 --> 00:02:07,034
to the bars.

63
00:02:07,094 --> 00:02:09,099
Nobody goes the long way round.

64
00:02:09,159 --> 00:02:11,535
It is about fifty metres long.

65
00:02:11,595 --> 00:02:13,275
That is a short walk.

66
00:02:13,335 --> 00:02:15,274
Twenty-five seconds, at a normal pace,

67
00:02:15,275 --> 00:02:16,733
without stopping.

68
00:02:16,793 --> 00:02:19,587
At the top it is about five metres across.

69
00:02:19,647 --> 00:02:20,807
At the bottom —

70
00:02:20,867 --> 00:02:23,161
the end that opens onto the main road —

71
00:02:23,167 --> 00:02:25,088
it is three point two.

72
00:02:25,148 --> 00:02:28,314
Three point two metres is two cars side by side.

73
00:02:28,374 --> 00:02:30,513
It is a living room, turned on its end

74
00:02:30,514 --> 00:02:32,979
and stretched out for fifty metres.

75
00:02:33,039 --> 00:02:35,898
A study published in 2024 by researchers writing

76
00:02:35,899 --> 00:02:38,678
in the journal PLOS One put the average width

77
00:02:38,679 --> 00:02:39,278
of that alley

78
00:02:39,279 --> 00:02:41,592
at under four metres along its length.

79
00:02:41,652 --> 00:02:43,517
And it is not flat.

80
00:02:43,577 --> 00:02:44,978
The street slopes.

81
00:02:45,038 --> 00:02:47,157
It rises from the main road up toward

82
00:02:47,158 --> 00:02:48,418
the streets behind,

83
00:02:48,478 --> 00:02:50,237
which means that anybody standing

84
00:02:50,238 --> 00:02:52,151
in it is standing on a hill.

85
00:02:52,211 --> 00:02:54,541
Nobody has published how steep.

86
00:02:54,601 --> 00:02:56,620
There is a figure for the width and a figure

87
00:02:56,621 --> 00:02:58,680
for the length and there is no figure

88
00:02:58,681 --> 00:02:59,741
for the gradient,

89
00:02:59,801 --> 00:03:01,860
so this film will not give you one.

90
00:03:01,913 --> 00:03:03,532
What it will tell you is the direction:

91
00:03:03,533 --> 00:03:06,193
up, away from the main road.

92
00:03:06,253 --> 00:03:08,992
That direction matters more than any number would,

93
00:03:08,993 --> 00:03:11,834
because it decides which way the weight goes.

94
00:03:11,894 --> 00:03:13,893
There is one more thing about the width,

95
00:03:13,894 --> 00:03:15,753
and it had been on file with the district

96
00:03:15,754 --> 00:03:17,242
for over a year.

97
00:03:17,302 --> 00:03:19,621
The Hamilton Hotel had illegally extended

98
00:03:19,622 --> 00:03:20,941
a terrace on the northern side

99
00:03:20,942 --> 00:03:22,562
of its main building —

100
00:03:22,622 --> 00:03:25,401
seventeen point two square metres of it —

101
00:03:25,402 --> 00:03:27,520
along the side that faces the alley.

102
00:03:27,540 --> 00:03:28,481
The Korea Times,

103
00:03:28,540 --> 00:03:31,019
reading the building records a few days after,

104
00:03:31,020 --> 00:03:32,599
wrote that the extension had made

105
00:03:32,600 --> 00:03:34,653
the narrow path even narrower.

106
00:03:34,713 --> 00:03:36,857
The district office already knew.

107
00:03:36,917 --> 00:03:38,996
It had notified the hotel of the violation

108
00:03:38,997 --> 00:03:41,290
and levied fines the previous year.

109
00:03:41,350 --> 00:03:42,369
So the state's knowledge

110
00:03:42,370 --> 00:03:44,423
of that street was not zero.

111
00:03:44,483 --> 00:03:46,116
Somebody had measured it.

112
00:03:46,176 --> 00:03:47,809
Somebody wrote it down.

113
00:03:47,869 --> 00:03:51,081
Somebody issued a penalty about it, in 2021.

114
00:03:51,141 --> 00:03:53,180
What nobody had done was ask what

115
00:03:53,181 --> 00:03:55,607
the street was for on a Saturday night.

116
00:03:55,667 --> 00:03:58,972
The date was the twenty-ninth of October, 2022.

117
00:03:59,032 --> 00:04:00,154
A Saturday.

118
00:04:00,214 --> 00:04:01,333
It was the first Halloween

119
00:04:01,334 --> 00:04:03,713
in three years without distancing rules,

120
00:04:03,714 --> 00:04:04,733
and the first

121
00:04:04,734 --> 00:04:07,420
with the outdoor mask requirement lifted.

122
00:04:07,480 --> 00:04:10,042
Itaewon is where that happens in Seoul.

123
00:04:10,102 --> 00:04:12,021
It is the district with the foreign restaurants

124
00:04:12,022 --> 00:04:13,742
and the bars that stay open,

125
00:04:13,802 --> 00:04:16,302
a few minutes from a station on two lines,

126
00:04:16,362 --> 00:04:18,461
and for one weekend a year it is where

127
00:04:18,462 --> 00:04:21,255
the whole city goes to be somewhere crowded.

128
00:04:21,315 --> 00:04:23,955
Al Jazeera, reporting three days later,

129
00:04:24,015 --> 00:04:24,574
put the number

130
00:04:24,575 --> 00:04:27,075
at an estimated hundred thousand people,

131
00:04:27,135 --> 00:04:28,914
many of them in their teens and twenties,

132
00:04:28,915 --> 00:04:30,611
and dressed in costume.

133
00:04:30,671 --> 00:04:33,510
A hundred thousand people is a stadium,

134
00:04:33,511 --> 00:04:35,610
arriving in one district, on foot,

135
00:04:35,611 --> 00:04:37,645
over about six hours, in the dark.

136
00:04:37,705 --> 00:04:39,570
The city knew how many.

137
00:04:39,630 --> 00:04:40,830
Not afterwards —

138
00:04:40,890 --> 00:04:41,609
that evening,

139
00:04:41,610 --> 00:04:43,969
in the ordinary course of running a railway.

140
00:04:43,970 --> 00:04:47,049
Eighty-one thousand five hundred

141
00:04:47,050 --> 00:04:50,569
and seventy-three people got off the train
at Itaewon station that day,

142
00:04:50,570 --> 00:04:52,582
on figures from Seoul Transportation Corporation.

143
00:04:52,583 --> 00:04:53,862
On the equivalent Saturday

144
00:04:53,863 --> 00:04:57,692
a year earlier it had been thirty-one thousand

145
00:04:57,752 --> 00:05:00,321
eight hundred and seventy-eight.
Two point six times as many.

146
00:05:00,381 --> 00:05:03,268
And they arrived in a curve anybody could read.

147
00:05:03,328 --> 00:05:06,800
Ten thousand seven hundred and forty-seven

148
00:05:06,860 --> 00:05:10,951
between six and seven.
Eleven thousand eight hundred and seventy-three

149
00:05:11,011 --> 00:05:13,816
between seven and eight.
Eleven thousand six hundred and sixty-six

150
00:05:13,817 --> 00:05:15,406
between eight and nine.

151
00:05:15,466 --> 00:05:16,825
One stop from that alley,

152
00:05:16,826 --> 00:05:18,385
a state-owned company was counting them

153
00:05:18,386 --> 00:05:20,489
as they came, hour by hour.

154
00:05:20,549 --> 00:05:22,182
Nobody organised it.

155
00:05:22,242 --> 00:05:25,182
There was no ticket, no promoter, no stage,

156
00:05:25,242 --> 00:05:27,590
no permit, no name on anything.

157
00:05:27,650 --> 00:05:28,589
Hold on to that,

158
00:05:28,590 --> 00:05:30,569
because in two years' time a court is going

159
00:05:30,570 --> 00:05:32,255
to build an acquittal on it.

160
00:05:32,315 --> 00:05:34,734
By the middle of the evening the alley was full,

161
00:05:34,735 --> 00:05:36,895
and it was full in both directions:

162
00:05:36,955 --> 00:05:39,314
people coming up from the station at the bottom,

163
00:05:39,315 --> 00:05:41,775
and people coming down from the streets
at the top,

164
00:05:41,835 --> 00:05:44,909
in a passage that narrows as it descends.

165
00:05:44,969 --> 00:05:46,369
Remember that too.

166
00:05:46,429 --> 00:05:47,830
Both directions.

167
00:05:47,890 --> 00:05:48,489
It is going

168
00:05:48,490 --> 00:05:51,241
to turn out to be the whole mechanism.

169
00:05:51,301 --> 00:05:53,301
At thirty-four minutes past six,

170
00:05:53,361 --> 00:05:55,320
somebody in it decided that this was a matter

171
00:05:55,321 --> 00:05:58,103
for the police.

172
00:05:58,163 --> 00:06:00,062
Between six thirty-four in the evening

173
00:06:00,063 --> 00:06:02,702
and eleven minutes past ten, the police

174
00:06:02,703 --> 00:06:05,022
in Itaewon received eleven distress reports

175
00:06:05,023 --> 00:06:07,737
about dangerous levels of overcrowding.

176
00:06:07,797 --> 00:06:09,896
That is the sentence the Korea Times printed

177
00:06:09,897 --> 00:06:11,377
in March of this year,

178
00:06:11,437 --> 00:06:13,416
reporting an investigative hearing,

179
00:06:13,417 --> 00:06:15,196
and it is worth taking apart slowly,

180
00:06:15,197 --> 00:06:18,254
because every word in it is doing work.

181
00:06:18,314 --> 00:06:19,994
Eleven reports.

182
00:06:20,054 --> 00:06:21,687
Not noise complaints.

183
00:06:21,747 --> 00:06:24,306
Reports about dangerous levels of overcrowding,

184
00:06:24,307 --> 00:06:27,374
made to the police, by the people standing in it.

185
00:06:27,434 --> 00:06:28,928
Here is the first one.

186
00:06:28,988 --> 00:06:30,627
Looks like you can get crushed to death

187
00:06:30,628 --> 00:06:32,207
with people keep coming up here

188
00:06:32,208 --> 00:06:35,033
while there's no room for people to go down.

189
00:06:35,093 --> 00:06:36,412
I barely managed to leave

190
00:06:36,413 --> 00:06:38,253
but there are too many people,

191
00:06:38,313 --> 00:06:40,607
looks like you should come and control.

192
00:06:40,641 --> 00:06:43,946
That is a translation, and it is worth saying so.

193
00:06:44,006 --> 00:06:46,150
The caller was speaking Korean.

194
00:06:46,210 --> 00:06:48,790
Different outlets rendered it differently —

195
00:06:48,850 --> 00:06:50,270
Al Jazeera published it

196
00:06:50,330 --> 00:06:52,209
as I feel like I would be almost crushed

197
00:06:52,210 --> 00:06:54,389
to death here because people continued

198
00:06:54,390 --> 00:06:57,503
to come up even though no more can go down.

199
00:06:57,563 --> 00:06:59,057
The wording moves.

200
00:06:59,117 --> 00:07:01,633
What does not move is the content.

201
00:07:01,693 --> 00:07:03,833
Four hours before anything happened,

202
00:07:03,893 --> 00:07:05,412
a person standing in that alley used

203
00:07:05,413 --> 00:07:06,592
the words crushed to death,

204
00:07:06,593 --> 00:07:09,503
and asked for somebody to come and control it.

205
00:07:09,563 --> 00:07:11,150
Officers were sent.

206
00:07:11,210 --> 00:07:11,889
That matters,

207
00:07:11,890 --> 00:07:13,969
and this film is going to be careful about it,

208
00:07:13,970 --> 00:07:15,589
because the easy version

209
00:07:15,590 --> 00:07:17,809
of this story is that nobody did anything,

210
00:07:17,810 --> 00:07:20,877
and the easy version is false.

211
00:07:20,937 --> 00:07:22,292
Officers went.

212
00:07:22,352 --> 00:07:24,462
They dispersed crowds where they went.

213
00:07:24,463 --> 00:07:26,402
The next call in the study's timeline came

214
00:07:26,403 --> 00:07:28,279
at nine minutes past eight.

215
00:07:28,339 --> 00:07:29,818
One hour and thirty-five minutes

216
00:07:29,819 --> 00:07:31,319
after the first one.

217
00:07:31,379 --> 00:07:33,418
There are people who fell over and got hurt

218
00:07:33,419 --> 00:07:35,474
because there are too many people.

219
00:07:35,534 --> 00:07:38,013
Read that as a piece of information arriving

220
00:07:38,014 --> 00:07:39,721
at a police switchboard.

221
00:07:39,781 --> 00:07:41,368
Not it is busy.

222
00:07:41,428 --> 00:07:43,201
Not it is uncomfortable.

223
00:07:43,261 --> 00:07:44,673
People have fallen over,

224
00:07:44,721 --> 00:07:45,960
and people have been hurt,

225
00:07:45,961 --> 00:07:48,609
and the reason given is the number of people.

226
00:07:48,669 --> 00:07:50,528
Two hours before anything was reported

227
00:07:50,529 --> 00:07:51,809
as an accident,

228
00:07:51,869 --> 00:07:54,309
the word fallen was already in the record.

229
00:07:54,310 --> 00:07:56,089
The calls kept coming, and the language

230
00:07:56,090 --> 00:07:58,544
in them stopped being about congestion.

231
00:07:58,604 --> 00:08:00,983
We are on the verge of a terrible accident due

232
00:08:00,984 --> 00:08:02,931
to the massive crowds.

233
00:08:02,991 --> 00:08:05,135
I am almost being crushed to death.

234
00:08:05,195 --> 00:08:06,474
Those are two different people,

235
00:08:06,475 --> 00:08:08,774
on two different calls, on the same evening,

236
00:08:08,775 --> 00:08:10,636
in the same street.

237
00:08:10,696 --> 00:08:12,115
The last of the eleven came

238
00:08:12,116 --> 00:08:14,140
in at eleven minutes past ten.

239
00:08:14,200 --> 00:08:15,647
Eleven calls.

240
00:08:15,707 --> 00:08:18,037
Officers were deployed to four of them.

241
00:08:18,097 --> 00:08:19,297
On the other seven,

242
00:08:19,357 --> 00:08:21,936
according to Al Jazeera's reporting at the time,

243
00:08:21,937 --> 00:08:23,492
there was no action.

244
00:08:23,552 --> 00:08:25,651
Three hours and thirty-seven minutes separate

245
00:08:25,652 --> 00:08:28,181
the first of those calls from the last one.

246
00:08:28,217 --> 00:08:28,816
Three hours

247
00:08:28,817 --> 00:08:30,376
and thirty-seven minutes is long enough

248
00:08:30,377 --> 00:08:32,451
to drive across a country.

249
00:08:32,511 --> 00:08:34,550
It is long enough that the shift you started

250
00:08:34,551 --> 00:08:37,130
the evening on is a different shift by the end

251
00:08:37,131 --> 00:08:37,952
of it.

252
00:08:38,012 --> 00:08:39,272
And across all of it,

253
00:08:39,332 --> 00:08:41,562
the width of the street did not change.

254
00:08:41,563 --> 00:08:44,443
The National Police Commissioner, Yoon Hee-keun,

255
00:08:44,503 --> 00:08:45,922
said afterwards that crowd control

256
00:08:45,923 --> 00:08:47,864
at the scene had been inadequate,

257
00:08:47,903 --> 00:08:49,742
and that there had been multiple reports

258
00:08:49,743 --> 00:08:51,622
to the police indicating the seriousness

259
00:08:51,623 --> 00:08:54,388
at the site just before the accident occurred.

260
00:08:54,448 --> 00:08:57,028
The Prime Minister, Han Duck-soo,

261
00:08:57,088 --> 00:08:59,647
said the police must conduct thorough inspections

262
00:08:59,648 --> 00:09:01,727
and provide a clear and transparent explanation

263
00:09:01,728 --> 00:09:02,954
to the public.

264
00:09:03,014 --> 00:09:04,513
There is a version of this story

265
00:09:04,514 --> 00:09:06,453
in which those eleven calls are the whole

266
00:09:06,454 --> 00:09:07,494
of the scandal,

267
00:09:07,554 --> 00:09:10,174
and that version is not quite right either.

268
00:09:10,234 --> 00:09:13,314
A call is information arriving at an organisation,

269
00:09:13,374 --> 00:09:15,753
and what an organisation does with it depends

270
00:09:15,754 --> 00:09:16,953
on what else it is doing

271
00:09:16,954 --> 00:09:19,808
and where its people are standing at the time.

272
00:09:19,868 --> 00:09:21,873
That is not an excuse.

273
00:09:21,933 --> 00:09:23,566
It is the next question.

274
00:09:23,626 --> 00:09:26,185
Both of those statements are true and neither

275
00:09:26,186 --> 00:09:27,365
of them is an answer,

276
00:09:27,366 --> 00:09:29,225
because neither of them says where

277
00:09:29,226 --> 00:09:30,693
the officers were.

278
00:09:30,753 --> 00:09:32,132
That answer took three years,

279
00:09:32,133 --> 00:09:35,883
and it did not come from the police.

280
00:09:35,943 --> 00:09:38,042
This film is not going to show you what happened

281
00:09:38,043 --> 00:09:41,042
in that street, and it is worth saying why rather

282
00:09:41,043 --> 00:09:42,452
than just doing it.

283
00:09:42,512 --> 00:09:44,994
A hundred and fifty-nine people died there.

284
00:09:44,995 --> 00:09:46,814
Their families are alive.

285
00:09:46,874 --> 00:09:48,433
Their names are in the public record

286
00:09:48,434 --> 00:09:50,876
and are not going to be in this film.

287
00:09:50,936 --> 00:09:52,655
So the street will appear three ways

288
00:09:52,656 --> 00:09:53,716
and no other way:

289
00:09:53,776 --> 00:09:56,749
empty, ordinarily busy, and afterwards.

290
00:09:56,809 --> 00:09:59,228
What can be described is the shape of the problem,

291
00:09:59,229 --> 00:10:02,204
and in this case somebody has measured it.

292
00:10:02,264 --> 00:10:05,423
In 2024 four researchers published a study

293
00:10:05,424 --> 00:10:07,944
of that night in PLOS One,

294
00:10:08,004 --> 00:10:10,272
reconstructing the crowd from the record.

295
00:10:10,273 --> 00:10:12,232
They put the average density during the crush

296
00:10:12,233 --> 00:10:15,852
at seven point five seven people per square metre,

297
00:10:15,853 --> 00:10:18,594
with a maximum of nine point nine five.

298
00:10:18,654 --> 00:10:20,752
One square metre is a doormat.

299
00:10:20,812 --> 00:10:22,167
Nine people.

300
00:10:22,227 --> 00:10:23,535
On a doormat.

301
00:10:23,595 --> 00:10:25,971
They calculated the pressure inside it.

302
00:10:26,031 --> 00:10:29,391
On average it peaked at one thousand

303
00:10:29,451 --> 00:10:33,435
and sixty-three newtons per metre, and at maximum,
one thousand nine hundred and sixty-one.

304
00:10:33,436 --> 00:10:36,335
Those are not numbers most people have a feel for,

305
00:10:36,336 --> 00:10:38,784
so here is the one that matters instead.

306
00:10:38,844 --> 00:10:40,643
In an area of eighteen square metres,

307
00:10:40,644 --> 00:10:44,166
the study records
that over three hundred people were concentrated.

308
00:10:44,206 --> 00:10:46,861
Eighteen square metres is a small bedroom.

309
00:10:46,921 --> 00:10:49,200
At the density those researchers measured,

310
00:10:49,201 --> 00:10:51,294
a person cannot lift their arms.

311
00:10:51,354 --> 00:10:53,650
They cannot choose where to put their feet.

312
00:10:53,651 --> 00:10:56,110
They are not standing in a crowd any more;

313
00:10:56,111 --> 00:10:57,510
they are part of one,

314
00:10:57,511 --> 00:10:59,570
and the direction they travel is decided

315
00:10:59,571 --> 00:11:01,100
by the people behind them.

316
00:11:01,149 --> 00:11:03,309
That is what those numbers describe:

317
00:11:03,369 --> 00:11:04,769
at the same headcount,

318
00:11:04,829 --> 00:11:06,968
a narrow sloping alley is a different kind

319
00:11:06,969 --> 00:11:09,562
of place from a wide flat one.

320
00:11:09,622 --> 00:11:11,901
And the mechanism they identify is the thing

321
00:11:11,902 --> 00:11:14,088
planted at the end of the first act.

322
00:11:14,148 --> 00:11:16,288
The primary causes, in their words,

323
00:11:16,348 --> 00:11:18,628
were the substantial population,

324
00:11:18,688 --> 00:11:21,808
bidirectional collision, and escalating panic —

325
00:11:21,868 --> 00:11:24,407
a bidirectional stream of pedestrians colliding

326
00:11:24,408 --> 00:11:25,859
in a narrow alley.

327
00:11:25,919 --> 00:11:27,738
People going up and people coming down,

328
00:11:27,739 --> 00:11:30,638
in a passage that gets narrower as it descends,

329
00:11:30,639 --> 00:11:31,918
on a hill.

330
00:11:31,978 --> 00:11:33,197
A crowd on flat ground

331
00:11:33,198 --> 00:11:36,618
that becomes too dense has one thing going for it:

332
00:11:36,678 --> 00:11:38,117
the pressure has somewhere to go,

333
00:11:38,118 --> 00:11:40,391
in every direction at once.

334
00:11:40,451 --> 00:11:41,590
A crowd in a passage

335
00:11:41,591 --> 00:11:44,030
between two buildings has two directions instead

336
00:11:44,031 --> 00:11:45,428
of every direction.

337
00:11:45,488 --> 00:11:47,307
A crowd being fed into that passage

338
00:11:47,308 --> 00:11:49,257
from both ends has none.

339
00:11:49,317 --> 00:11:52,297
And the incline decided which way the weight went.

340
00:11:52,357 --> 00:11:53,851
It went downward.

341
00:11:53,911 --> 00:11:56,050
The study's timeline puts the first report

342
00:11:56,051 --> 00:11:57,310
of a crushing accident,

343
00:11:57,311 --> 00:11:59,630
involving approximately ten people,

344
00:11:59,631 --> 00:12:02,510
at fifteen minutes past ten.

345
00:12:02,570 --> 00:12:04,949
Three minutes later, at eighteen minutes past,

346
00:12:04,950 --> 00:12:07,189
the police chief ordered all available personnel

347
00:12:07,190 --> 00:12:08,383
to the scene.

348
00:12:08,443 --> 00:12:10,442
The first emergency rescue team arrived

349
00:12:10,443 --> 00:12:12,863
at twenty-eight minutes past ten.

350
00:12:12,923 --> 00:12:14,510
Thirteen minutes.

351
00:12:14,570 --> 00:12:15,809
Written down like that,

352
00:12:15,810 --> 00:12:17,782
thirteen minutes is a short time.

353
00:12:17,842 --> 00:12:18,741
Measured against what

354
00:12:18,742 --> 00:12:20,901
the study says was happening inside eighteen

355
00:12:20,902 --> 00:12:24,212
square metres, it is not a short time at all.

356
00:12:24,272 --> 00:12:25,451
The next part is a count,

357
00:12:25,452 --> 00:12:27,763
and the count moved for two months.

358
00:12:27,823 --> 00:12:29,242
In the immediate aftermath,

359
00:12:29,243 --> 00:12:32,162
the figure reported was a hundred and fifty-seven.

360
00:12:32,163 --> 00:12:34,974
By the fourteenth of November it was a hundred

361
00:12:34,975 --> 00:12:35,666
and fifty-eight.

362
00:12:35,667 --> 00:12:38,296
By the third of January it was a hundred

363
00:12:38,297 --> 00:12:38,985
and fifty-nine.

364
00:12:38,986 --> 00:12:40,805
The last of them was a high-school student

365
00:12:40,806 --> 00:12:43,394
who had been in that street and survived it,

366
00:12:43,426 --> 00:12:45,325
found dead on the twelfth of December,

367
00:12:45,326 --> 00:12:48,045
and recognised by the Ministry of the Interior

368
00:12:48,046 --> 00:12:51,300
and Safety as a victim of the disaster.

369
00:12:51,360 --> 00:12:53,225
A hundred and fifty-nine.

370
00:12:53,285 --> 00:12:54,604
A further hundred

371
00:12:54,605 --> 00:12:56,370
and ninety-six people were injured.

372
00:12:56,371 --> 00:12:58,610
Reuters described the dead as mostly young people,

373
00:12:58,611 --> 00:13:00,090
and that is as far

374
00:13:00,091 --> 00:13:02,170
as this film will characterise them,

375
00:13:02,171 --> 00:13:03,631
with one exception,

376
00:13:03,691 --> 00:13:05,550
which is a matter of public record

377
00:13:05,551 --> 00:13:08,732
and is about countries rather than about people.

378
00:13:08,792 --> 00:13:10,711
Twenty-six of the a hundred

379
00:13:10,712 --> 00:13:13,138
and fifty-nine were foreign nationals,

380
00:13:13,198 --> 00:13:16,115
from fourteen countries.
Three years later, in October 2025,

381
00:13:16,175 --> 00:13:18,334
forty-six relatives of twenty-one

382
00:13:18,335 --> 00:13:21,314
of those twenty-six travelled to Seoul for a week,

383
00:13:21,315 --> 00:13:23,054
at the official invitation

384
00:13:23,055 --> 00:13:26,050
of the Korean government, and went to the site.

385
00:13:26,110 --> 00:13:28,254
They came from twelve nations.

386
00:13:28,314 --> 00:13:31,454
Iran, Russia, the United States, Australia, China,

387
00:13:31,514 --> 00:13:34,374
Japan, France, Austria, Norway, Sri Lanka,

388
00:13:34,434 --> 00:13:36,402
Kazakhstan, Uzbekistan.

389
00:13:36,462 --> 00:13:38,109
That is a list of countries,

390
00:13:38,122 --> 00:13:39,081
not a list of people,

391
00:13:39,082 --> 00:13:42,001
and it is the only list this film is going

392
00:13:42,002 --> 00:13:43,157
to read out.

393
00:13:43,217 --> 00:13:45,336
There is a second toll figure in circulation,

394
00:13:45,337 --> 00:13:48,194
and you may see it if you go looking.

395
00:13:48,254 --> 00:13:50,113
A study published in July of this year

396
00:13:50,114 --> 00:13:52,573
by the special investigation commission works

397
00:13:52,574 --> 00:13:54,717
from a slightly larger set.

398
00:13:54,777 --> 00:13:56,077
The official figure,

399
00:13:56,137 --> 00:13:57,596
recorded by the ministry and carried

400
00:13:57,597 --> 00:14:00,915
by the reporting, is a hundred and fifty-nine.

401
00:14:00,975 --> 00:14:03,769
Until that changes, this film uses it.

402
00:14:03,829 --> 00:14:05,128
That study is worth knowing

403
00:14:05,129 --> 00:14:06,995
about for a different reason.

404
00:14:07,055 --> 00:14:08,514
It was carried out by the Department

405
00:14:08,515 --> 00:14:09,674
of Forensic Medicine

406
00:14:09,675 --> 00:14:12,715
at Pusan National University School of Medicine,

407
00:14:12,775 --> 00:14:14,657
working from death certificates,

408
00:14:14,715 --> 00:14:17,233
post-mortem reports and medical records.

409
00:14:17,293 --> 00:14:18,792
It found that about one in ten

410
00:14:18,793 --> 00:14:21,172
of the dead may not have died of asphyxiation

411
00:14:21,173 --> 00:14:22,273
at all —

412
00:14:22,333 --> 00:14:24,712
that the cause may have been crush syndrome,

413
00:14:24,713 --> 00:14:26,193
or rhabdomyolysis,

414
00:14:26,253 --> 00:14:28,959
or damage to internal organs from compression.

415
00:14:29,017 --> 00:14:31,440
The distinction is not academic.

416
00:14:31,500 --> 00:14:33,412
Asphyxiation is fast.

417
00:14:33,472 --> 00:14:35,012
The others are not.

418
00:14:35,072 --> 00:14:36,411
And the commission's conclusion

419
00:14:36,412 --> 00:14:39,071
from it was that more people might have survived

420
00:14:39,072 --> 00:14:41,051
if rescue efforts had continued immediately

421
00:14:41,052 --> 00:14:42,510
after the incident.

422
00:14:42,570 --> 00:14:45,290
That is their finding, published in 2026,

423
00:14:45,350 --> 00:14:47,141
three and a half years afterwards.

424
00:14:47,142 --> 00:14:49,422
It is theirs and not this film's,

425
00:14:49,482 --> 00:14:51,521
and this film is not going to extend it

426
00:14:51,522 --> 00:14:53,841
into a sentence about what would have happened,

427
00:14:53,842 --> 00:14:55,960
because nobody has established that.

428
00:14:55,987 --> 00:14:58,346
By the morning of the thirtieth of October,

429
00:14:58,347 --> 00:15:00,082
the street was open again.

430
00:15:00,142 --> 00:15:01,581
Which leaves the question the rest

431
00:15:01,582 --> 00:15:03,022
of this is about:

432
00:15:03,082 --> 00:15:04,141
on a Saturday night,

433
00:15:04,142 --> 00:15:06,902
in a district that fills up every Halloween,

434
00:15:06,962 --> 00:15:09,301
in a city with one of the largest police forces

435
00:15:09,302 --> 00:15:13,771
in the world, where were the officers?

436
00:15:13,831 --> 00:15:15,650
A hundred and thirty-seven.

437
00:15:15,710 --> 00:15:18,069
That is the number of police officers deployed

438
00:15:18,070 --> 00:15:19,910
to Itaewon for Halloween,

439
00:15:19,970 --> 00:15:22,409
as the police themselves had previously said,

440
00:15:22,410 --> 00:15:25,424
and as Al Jazeera reported three days afterwards.

441
00:15:25,484 --> 00:15:25,923
A hundred

442
00:15:25,924 --> 00:15:28,743
and thirty-seven officers is a real deployment.

443
00:15:28,803 --> 00:15:31,062
Spread across a district of bars and restaurants

444
00:15:31,063 --> 00:15:32,523
on its busiest night,

445
00:15:32,583 --> 00:15:35,230
against an estimated hundred thousand people,

446
00:15:35,263 --> 00:15:38,102
most of them working on crime rather than crowds,

447
00:15:38,103 --> 00:15:40,096
it is also not very many.

448
00:15:40,156 --> 00:15:43,333
That is one officer for every seven hundred

449
00:15:43,393 --> 00:15:46,264
and thirty people.
The obvious question is why there were not more,

450
00:15:46,265 --> 00:15:47,844
and for three years

451
00:15:47,845 --> 00:15:50,680
the obvious question had no official answer.

452
00:15:50,740 --> 00:15:54,184
It got one on the twenty-third of October, 2025.

453
00:15:54,244 --> 00:15:56,423
On that date the Korea Times reported the findings

454
00:15:56,424 --> 00:15:57,343
of a joint audit,

455
00:15:57,344 --> 00:15:59,083
carried out together by the Office

456
00:15:59,084 --> 00:16:01,264
for Government Policy Coordination,

457
00:16:01,324 --> 00:16:02,984
the National Police Agency,

458
00:16:03,044 --> 00:16:05,456
and the Ministry of the Interior and Safety.

459
00:16:05,457 --> 00:16:06,877
Three government bodies,

460
00:16:06,937 --> 00:16:08,796
including the police themselves,

461
00:16:08,797 --> 00:16:10,945
auditing what the police had done.

462
00:16:11,005 --> 00:16:13,474
And what they found was about a building.

463
00:16:13,534 --> 00:16:16,433
In 2022, the President of South Korea moved

464
00:16:16,434 --> 00:16:18,232
the presidential office.

465
00:16:18,292 --> 00:16:20,791
It left the compound it had occupied for decades

466
00:16:20,792 --> 00:16:22,772
and moved into Yongsan —

467
00:16:22,832 --> 00:16:24,692
the same district as Itaewon,

468
00:16:24,752 --> 00:16:27,368
a little over two kilometres from that alley.

469
00:16:27,369 --> 00:16:30,303
A presidential office is more than a building.

470
00:16:30,363 --> 00:16:32,382
It is a place people come to be heard outside

471
00:16:32,383 --> 00:16:33,250
of.

472
00:16:33,310 --> 00:16:35,029
Rallies and demonstrations inside

473
00:16:35,030 --> 00:16:37,729
the Yongsan police station's jurisdiction went

474
00:16:37,730 --> 00:16:39,769
from thirty-four in the whole of 2021

475
00:16:39,770 --> 00:16:42,909
to nine hundred and twenty-one

476
00:16:42,910 --> 00:16:44,569
between May and October of 2022.

477
00:16:44,570 --> 00:16:46,110
Thirty-four in a year.

478
00:16:46,170 --> 00:16:48,871
Nine hundred and twenty-one in six months.

479
00:16:48,931 --> 00:16:51,539
That is not a rounding error in a workload.

480
00:16:51,599 --> 00:16:53,743
That is a different job.

481
00:16:53,803 --> 00:16:54,662
Police resources

482
00:16:54,663 --> 00:16:56,142
in the district had been redirected

483
00:16:56,143 --> 00:16:57,502
to the Samgakji area,

484
00:16:57,503 --> 00:16:59,848
near the presidential office.

485
00:16:59,908 --> 00:17:01,614
And the audit's own sentence,

486
00:17:01,628 --> 00:17:04,235
three years after the fact, was this.

487
00:17:04,295 --> 00:17:06,554
The relocation of the presidential office

488
00:17:06,555 --> 00:17:08,654
to Yongsan increased the demand

489
00:17:08,655 --> 00:17:10,654
for police deployment in the area,

490
00:17:10,655 --> 00:17:12,694
which was a key factor behind the lack

491
00:17:12,695 --> 00:17:15,123
of crowd control officers in Itaewon.

492
00:17:15,183 --> 00:17:16,203
Read it slowly,

493
00:17:16,263 --> 00:17:18,502
because it is the closest thing in this story

494
00:17:18,503 --> 00:17:20,253
to a structural answer.

495
00:17:20,313 --> 00:17:21,952
Nobody in that sentence decided

496
00:17:21,953 --> 00:17:23,832
that Itaewon should be short of officers

497
00:17:23,833 --> 00:17:25,058
on Halloween.

498
00:17:25,118 --> 00:17:26,844
Nobody wrote that down.

499
00:17:26,904 --> 00:17:28,305
Nobody signed it.

500
00:17:28,365 --> 00:17:30,144
A government made a decision about where

501
00:17:30,145 --> 00:17:31,856
a president should sit.

502
00:17:31,916 --> 00:17:33,995
That decision created a standing demand

503
00:17:33,996 --> 00:17:36,290
for officers in one part of a district.

504
00:17:36,349 --> 00:17:39,388
The officers came from the same place all officers

505
00:17:39,389 --> 00:17:41,512
in that district come from.

506
00:17:41,572 --> 00:17:43,551
And on the last Saturday in October,

507
00:17:43,552 --> 00:17:45,251
in the other part of the district,

508
00:17:45,252 --> 00:17:47,487
there were a hundred and thirty-seven.

509
00:17:47,538 --> 00:17:48,977
This film is not going to tell you

510
00:17:48,978 --> 00:17:51,157
that more officers would have changed the outcome,

511
00:17:51,158 --> 00:17:53,538
because nobody has established that,

512
00:17:53,598 --> 00:17:56,917
and a film that says would have about a hundred

513
00:17:56,918 --> 00:17:58,843
and fifty-nine deaths is making something up.

514
00:17:58,844 --> 00:18:01,267
What can be said is narrower and worse.

515
00:18:01,327 --> 00:18:02,666
Eleven people called the number

516
00:18:02,667 --> 00:18:05,236
the state gives you for exactly this.

517
00:18:05,296 --> 00:18:07,301
Four of those calls were attended.

518
00:18:07,361 --> 00:18:10,340
And the reason the district was thin
that night has now been written down

519
00:18:10,341 --> 00:18:12,280
by the government itself, three years later,

520
00:18:12,281 --> 00:18:15,310
in a document it published about its own conduct.

521
00:18:15,370 --> 00:18:17,549
Three years is a long time for a sentence like

522
00:18:17,550 --> 00:18:18,814
that to take.

523
00:18:18,874 --> 00:18:20,213
By the time it was published,

524
00:18:20,214 --> 00:18:21,993
the courts had already finished with it,

525
00:18:21,994 --> 00:18:24,362
and so had the Constitutional Court.

526
00:18:24,422 --> 00:18:26,101
There is one more official document

527
00:18:26,102 --> 00:18:27,541
about that night.

528
00:18:27,601 --> 00:18:29,400
It came two years before the audit,

529
00:18:29,401 --> 00:18:31,696
and it says the opposite of it.

530
00:18:31,756 --> 00:18:34,315
In February 2023, the National Assembly voted

531
00:18:34,316 --> 00:18:36,136
to impeach Lee Sang-min,

532
00:18:36,196 --> 00:18:37,655
the Interior and Safety Minister,

533
00:18:37,656 --> 00:18:39,287
over the disaster.

534
00:18:39,347 --> 00:18:41,406
On the twenty-fifth of July that year,

535
00:18:41,407 --> 00:18:42,246
all nine judges

536
00:18:42,247 --> 00:18:44,066
of the Constitutional Court rejected

537
00:18:44,067 --> 00:18:45,866
the impeachment, unanimously,

538
00:18:45,867 --> 00:18:48,829
and he was reinstated as minister.

539
00:18:48,889 --> 00:18:51,108
The court's reasoning was that the emergency

540
00:18:51,109 --> 00:18:52,608
response system used to handle

541
00:18:52,609 --> 00:18:55,769
the incident was not significantly deficient,

542
00:18:55,829 --> 00:18:58,476
given the communication between the ministry,

543
00:18:58,509 --> 00:19:00,566
the police and the district office.

544
00:19:00,567 --> 00:19:01,606
Hold that sentence next

545
00:19:01,607 --> 00:19:03,699
to the audit you heard two minutes ago.

546
00:19:03,700 --> 00:19:05,983
Not significantly deficient.

547
00:19:06,043 --> 00:19:06,382
And:

548
00:19:06,383 --> 00:19:08,442
a key factor behind the lack

549
00:19:08,443 --> 00:19:10,881
of crowd control officers in Itaewon.

550
00:19:10,941 --> 00:19:12,388
Both are official.

551
00:19:12,448 --> 00:19:13,988
Both are in writing.

552
00:19:14,048 --> 00:19:15,960
They describe the same night.

553
00:19:16,020 --> 00:19:17,793
They are two years apart.

554
00:19:17,853 --> 00:19:18,412
And in March

555
00:19:18,413 --> 00:19:21,373
of this year one more person said it out loud,

556
00:19:21,433 --> 00:19:24,223
at a hearing, under his own name.

557
00:19:24,283 --> 00:19:26,283
On the twelfth of March, 2026,

558
00:19:26,343 --> 00:19:27,962
the special investigation commission held

559
00:19:27,963 --> 00:19:30,746
an investigative hearing in central Seoul.

560
00:19:30,806 --> 00:19:31,966
Lee Im-jae —

561
00:19:32,026 --> 00:19:33,205
the former station chief,

562
00:19:33,206 --> 00:19:36,526
convicted at first instance in September 2024,

563
00:19:36,586 --> 00:19:39,626
his appeal suspended since July 2025 —

564
00:19:39,686 --> 00:19:41,170
appeared as a witness.

565
00:19:41,230 --> 00:19:41,649
He said

566
00:19:41,650 --> 00:19:43,849
that if the presidential office had not been moved

567
00:19:43,850 --> 00:19:46,789
to Yongsan, he thought the possibility of such

568
00:19:46,790 --> 00:19:49,429
a terrible accident would have been considerably

569
00:19:49,430 --> 00:19:50,433
lower.

570
00:19:50,493 --> 00:19:51,712
He said that with a great deal

571
00:19:51,713 --> 00:19:54,152
of manpower dispersed to the presidential office,

572
00:19:54,153 --> 00:19:56,413
and fatigue accumulating,

573
00:19:56,473 --> 00:19:58,906
response capability had been degraded.

574
00:19:58,966 --> 00:20:01,465
That is his account, given four years afterwards,

575
00:20:01,466 --> 00:20:04,314
by a man with a conviction to appeal against.

576
00:20:04,374 --> 00:20:06,286
This film does not adopt it.

577
00:20:06,346 --> 00:20:08,006
It reports that he said it —

578
00:20:08,066 --> 00:20:08,525
and notes

579
00:20:08,526 --> 00:20:10,765
that the government's own audit had already said

580
00:20:10,766 --> 00:20:14,727
the first half of it, five months earlier.

581
00:20:14,787 --> 00:20:17,407
On the thirtieth of September, 2024,

582
00:20:17,467 --> 00:20:19,326
the Seoul Western District Court delivered

583
00:20:19,327 --> 00:20:20,786
its judgment on the officials

584
00:20:20,787 --> 00:20:22,934
who had been indicted over that night.

585
00:20:22,935 --> 00:20:23,354
Everything

586
00:20:23,355 --> 00:20:26,194
that follows is a first-instance judgment.

587
00:20:26,254 --> 00:20:28,154
Lee Im-jae, then fifty-four,

588
00:20:28,214 --> 00:20:30,593
the former chief of the Yongsan police station,

589
00:20:30,594 --> 00:20:32,733
was sentenced at first instance that day

590
00:20:32,734 --> 00:20:34,713
to three years in prison without labour,

591
00:20:34,714 --> 00:20:37,833
on charges of professional negligence resulting

592
00:20:37,834 --> 00:20:39,451
in death and injury.

593
00:20:39,511 --> 00:20:40,805
The court's reasoning:

594
00:20:40,851 --> 00:20:42,170
it was either foreseen

595
00:20:42,171 --> 00:20:43,790
or it could have been anticipated

596
00:20:43,791 --> 00:20:45,590
that a large crowd of people gathering

597
00:20:45,591 --> 00:20:48,170
at the slanted alleyway in Itaewon

598
00:20:48,171 --> 00:20:50,830
for the 2022 Halloween could cause

599
00:20:50,831 --> 00:20:52,330
a serious danger to bodies

600
00:20:52,331 --> 00:20:54,101
from pedestrians pushing.

601
00:20:54,161 --> 00:20:56,340
The court found that he had neglected to establish

602
00:20:56,341 --> 00:20:58,360
and implement a safety management plan

603
00:20:58,361 --> 00:20:59,556
to prevent it.

604
00:20:59,616 --> 00:21:01,675
Two others from the same station were sentenced

605
00:21:01,676 --> 00:21:02,816
that day:

606
00:21:02,876 --> 00:21:04,656
Song Byung-ju,

607
00:21:04,716 --> 00:21:06,695
who headed its one-one-two situation room,

608
00:21:06,696 --> 00:21:08,455
to two years without labour,

609
00:21:08,456 --> 00:21:11,115
and a situation team leader to one year,

610
00:21:11,116 --> 00:21:12,441
suspended.

611
00:21:12,501 --> 00:21:14,220
He was acquitted at first instance

612
00:21:14,221 --> 00:21:15,741
on the other charges:

613
00:21:15,801 --> 00:21:17,340
perjury before the National Assembly,

614
00:21:17,341 --> 00:21:19,753
and a false official document.

615
00:21:19,813 --> 00:21:22,048
And then the same court, the same day,

616
00:21:22,093 --> 00:21:23,446
turned to the district.

617
00:21:23,503 --> 00:21:24,963
Park Hee-young,

618
00:21:25,023 --> 00:21:26,762
the chief of the Yongsan ward office,

619
00:21:26,763 --> 00:21:30,012
and other ward officials, were also indicted.

620
00:21:30,072 --> 00:21:32,541
The same court found them not guilty.

621
00:21:32,601 --> 00:21:34,466
Not insufficient evidence.

622
00:21:34,526 --> 00:21:36,484
Not we cannot be sure.

623
00:21:36,544 --> 00:21:38,684
Something more specific than that,

624
00:21:38,744 --> 00:21:39,863
and it is the sentence

625
00:21:39,864 --> 00:21:42,184
this whole film has been walking toward.

626
00:21:42,185 --> 00:21:44,844
Related law and regulations did not require them

627
00:21:44,845 --> 00:21:46,164
to come up with safety measures

628
00:21:46,165 --> 00:21:48,230
for events without organizers.

629
00:21:48,290 --> 00:21:48,649
And:

630
00:21:48,650 --> 00:21:51,649
there were no obligatory regulations specifying

631
00:21:51,650 --> 00:21:52,129
the need

632
00:21:52,130 --> 00:21:54,846
to establish separate safety management plans.

633
00:21:54,906 --> 00:21:56,566
In the court's own language:

634
00:21:56,626 --> 00:21:58,865
it was hard to find that she bore a specific

635
00:21:58,866 --> 00:22:01,385
and direct duty of care to supplement

636
00:22:01,386 --> 00:22:04,806
a safety management plan for Halloween 2022.

637
00:22:04,866 --> 00:22:07,289
That is not a loophole somebody found.

638
00:22:07,349 --> 00:22:09,168
It is what the law said.

639
00:22:09,228 --> 00:22:12,147
Under South Korea's framework law on disaster

640
00:22:12,148 --> 00:22:14,767
and safety management, a voluntary event

641
00:22:14,768 --> 00:22:16,927
with no organiser did not have to file

642
00:22:16,928 --> 00:22:18,608
a safety plan in advance,

643
00:22:18,668 --> 00:22:20,347
and it was ambiguous where responsibility

644
00:22:20,348 --> 00:22:21,867
on the ground sat.

645
00:22:21,927 --> 00:22:23,456
Until the law was revised,

646
00:22:23,467 --> 00:22:25,966
it set out administrative duty and liability

647
00:22:25,967 --> 00:22:28,987
for official events and for local festivals —

648
00:22:29,047 --> 00:22:31,827
the ones where it was clear whose event it was.

649
00:22:31,887 --> 00:22:34,786
A hundred thousand people walking into a district

650
00:22:34,787 --> 00:22:36,026
because it is the twenty-ninth

651
00:22:36,027 --> 00:22:39,232
of October is not anybody's event.

652
00:22:39,292 --> 00:22:41,065
There is no form for it.

653
00:22:41,125 --> 00:22:43,725
And so, in the judgment of that court,

654
00:22:43,785 --> 00:22:46,102
there was no duty attached to it.

655
00:22:46,162 --> 00:22:47,888
There is now.

656
00:22:47,948 --> 00:22:52,187
Article sixty-six dash eleven of the Framework Act

657
00:22:52,188 --> 00:22:54,307
on the Management of Disasters

658
00:22:54,308 --> 00:22:56,987
and Safety is titled safety management measures

659
00:22:56,988 --> 00:23:01,259
when holding a local festival.
It was inserted into that act in 2013.

660
00:23:01,319 --> 00:23:03,679
On the twenty-sixth of December, 2023,

661
00:23:03,739 --> 00:23:05,646
its first paragraph was amended.

662
00:23:05,706 --> 00:23:08,385
Where a local festival at which the participation

663
00:23:08,386 --> 00:23:10,925
of a crowd is expected has no organiser,

664
00:23:10,926 --> 00:23:14,005
or its organiser is unclear, the head

665
00:23:14,006 --> 00:23:16,585
of the competent local government shall establish

666
00:23:16,586 --> 00:23:19,686
a local-festival safety management plan,

667
00:23:19,746 --> 00:23:21,685
taking into account the expected scale

668
00:23:21,686 --> 00:23:23,779
of participants and the venue.

669
00:23:23,839 --> 00:23:25,286
That is the sentence.

670
00:23:25,346 --> 00:23:27,105
On the night this film is about,

671
00:23:27,106 --> 00:23:28,790
it was not law.

672
00:23:28,850 --> 00:23:30,529
One thing about the order of those dates,

673
00:23:30,530 --> 00:23:33,409
because it is easy to get backwards.

674
00:23:33,469 --> 00:23:36,168
The amendment was already law in September 2024,

675
00:23:36,169 --> 00:23:38,539
when the court delivered the acquittal.

676
00:23:38,599 --> 00:23:40,479
The court was not ignoring it:

677
00:23:40,539 --> 00:23:42,718
a criminal court applies the law as it stood

678
00:23:42,719 --> 00:23:43,659
on the night,

679
00:23:43,719 --> 00:23:46,455
and on that night the sentence did not exist.

680
00:23:46,515 --> 00:23:47,594
The law now knows

681
00:23:47,595 --> 00:23:50,474
that a crowd can happen without anybody calling it

682
00:23:50,475 --> 00:23:51,538
an event.

683
00:23:51,598 --> 00:23:53,818
It learned that in December 2023,

684
00:23:53,878 --> 00:23:55,367
fourteen months late.

685
00:23:55,427 --> 00:23:58,082
The act says who has to write the plan.

686
00:23:58,142 --> 00:23:59,402
A second document,

687
00:23:59,462 --> 00:24:01,301
the enforcement decree of the same act,

688
00:24:01,302 --> 00:24:03,444
says what has to be in it.

689
00:24:03,504 --> 00:24:05,787
Article seventy-three dash nine.

690
00:24:05,847 --> 00:24:07,987
Where a festival has no organiser,

691
00:24:08,047 --> 00:24:10,027
or its organiser is unclear,

692
00:24:10,087 --> 00:24:11,786
the plan is written by the mayor,

693
00:24:11,787 --> 00:24:12,963
the county governor,

694
00:24:12,967 --> 00:24:15,375
or the district head with jurisdiction.

695
00:24:15,435 --> 00:24:17,951
And the plan has to contain five things.

696
00:24:18,011 --> 00:24:19,691
An outline of the event.

697
00:24:19,751 --> 00:24:22,330
The person responsible for safety management,

698
00:24:22,331 --> 00:24:25,378
the organisation that manages it, and its duties.

699
00:24:25,438 --> 00:24:27,777
Measures to prevent loss of life from fire

700
00:24:27,778 --> 00:24:29,904
and from crowd concentration.

701
00:24:29,964 --> 00:24:31,023
A plan for securing

702
00:24:31,024 --> 00:24:33,594
and deploying safety-management personnel.

703
00:24:33,654 --> 00:24:35,393
And emergency response procedures,

704
00:24:35,394 --> 00:24:38,677
with the contact details of the relevant agencies.

705
00:24:38,737 --> 00:24:40,324
That is the list.

706
00:24:40,384 --> 00:24:42,123
There is nothing clever in it.

707
00:24:42,124 --> 00:24:42,763
Every line

708
00:24:42,764 --> 00:24:44,803
of it is something somebody has to decide

709
00:24:44,804 --> 00:24:48,123
in advance, on paper, with their name on it.

710
00:24:48,183 --> 00:24:50,142
This film is not going to tell you what such

711
00:24:50,143 --> 00:24:52,222
a plan would have done on the twenty-ninth

712
00:24:52,223 --> 00:24:54,422
of October, 2022,

713
00:24:54,423 --> 00:24:56,783
because nobody has established that,

714
00:24:56,843 --> 00:24:59,429
and it is not a thing anybody can know.

715
00:24:59,489 --> 00:25:02,049
What can be said is that it exists now,

716
00:25:02,109 --> 00:25:03,989
that it did not exist then,

717
00:25:04,049 --> 00:25:05,628
and that it is written in the language

718
00:25:05,629 --> 00:25:06,609
of the night:

719
00:25:06,669 --> 00:25:12,009
fire, crowd concentration, personnel, deployment,

720
00:25:12,069 --> 00:25:13,475
responsibility.

721
00:25:13,535 --> 00:25:15,653
The duty is still missing something.

722
00:25:15,693 --> 00:25:17,192
In April of this year a member

723
00:25:17,193 --> 00:25:19,332
of the National Assembly proposed adding

724
00:25:19,333 --> 00:25:20,633
a penalty —

725
00:25:20,693 --> 00:25:23,592
an administrative fine of up to two million won

726
00:25:23,593 --> 00:25:26,052
for failing to file one of those plans,

727
00:25:26,053 --> 00:25:27,212
and a power to demand

728
00:25:27,213 --> 00:25:29,215
that a bad plan be improved.

729
00:25:29,275 --> 00:25:31,934
The reason given was that the duty was already

730
00:25:31,935 --> 00:25:34,574
a legal obligation, and there was no basis

731
00:25:34,575 --> 00:25:37,178
on which to sanction anybody who ignored it.

732
00:25:37,238 --> 00:25:39,737
Three and a half years after a hundred

733
00:25:39,738 --> 00:25:41,297
and fifty-nine people died in a street

734
00:25:41,298 --> 00:25:45,117
that belonged to nobody, the rule exists —

735
00:25:45,118 --> 00:25:47,382
and the penalty for ignoring it was still a bill.

736
00:25:47,383 --> 00:25:50,102
Kim Kwang-ho, the former Seoul police chief

737
00:25:50,103 --> 00:25:51,742
and the highest-ranking officer indicted

738
00:25:51,743 --> 00:25:53,023
over that night,

739
00:25:53,083 --> 00:25:56,403
was acquitted on the seventeenth of October, 2024,

740
00:25:56,463 --> 00:25:58,815
along with two other police officers.

741
00:25:58,875 --> 00:25:59,934
The court said it was hard

742
00:25:59,935 --> 00:26:01,674
to establish beyond reasonable doubt,

743
00:26:01,675 --> 00:26:04,334
with the evidence put forward by the prosecution,

744
00:26:04,335 --> 00:26:06,714
that the defendants committed professional

745
00:26:06,715 --> 00:26:08,031
negligence.

746
00:26:08,091 --> 00:26:10,431
On the seventh of October, 2024,

747
00:26:10,491 --> 00:26:11,953
prosecutors appealed.

748
00:26:12,013 --> 00:26:14,552
They appealed against the former station chief,

749
00:26:14,553 --> 00:26:15,712
the district office chief,

750
00:26:15,713 --> 00:26:17,408
and seven other officials.

751
00:26:17,468 --> 00:26:19,928
Their grounds, as reported by MBC,

752
00:26:19,988 --> 00:26:21,987
were that the defendants were shifting the blame

753
00:26:21,988 --> 00:26:24,328
and not seriously reflecting,

754
00:26:24,388 --> 00:26:26,727
and that the court had misapprehended the law

755
00:26:26,728 --> 00:26:29,407
on the district chief's duty under the disaster

756
00:26:29,408 --> 00:26:30,850
and safety act.

757
00:26:30,910 --> 00:26:33,150
And then, in the summer of 2025,

758
00:26:33,210 --> 00:26:34,540
both appeals stopped.

759
00:26:34,600 --> 00:26:36,001
Not concluded.

760
00:26:36,061 --> 00:26:37,276
Stopped.

761
00:26:37,336 --> 00:26:38,830
By the court itself.

762
00:26:38,890 --> 00:26:41,370
On the fourteenth of July, 2025,

763
00:26:41,430 --> 00:26:42,889
the thirteenth criminal division

764
00:26:42,890 --> 00:26:45,589
of the Seoul High Court suspended the appeal

765
00:26:45,590 --> 00:26:47,769
of the former station chief and the two officers

766
00:26:47,770 --> 00:26:49,904
from his one-one-two room.

767
00:26:49,964 --> 00:26:50,323
If what

768
00:26:50,324 --> 00:26:52,963
the special committee is doing is re-investigating

769
00:26:52,964 --> 00:26:54,864
the facts, the bench said,

770
00:26:54,924 --> 00:26:57,542
then it is right to try the case afterwards.

771
00:26:57,602 --> 00:26:59,341
There are still many unresolved matters

772
00:26:59,342 --> 00:27:00,702
from the disaster,

773
00:27:00,762 --> 00:27:02,941
and if there is no integrated resolution

774
00:27:02,942 --> 00:27:05,702
and the procedures become fragmented,

775
00:27:05,762 --> 00:27:08,337
the harm to the victims is aggravated.

776
00:27:08,397 --> 00:27:10,976
Six weeks later, on the twenty-eighth of August,

777
00:27:10,977 --> 00:27:14,408
a different bench did the same
with the district office chief's appeal.

778
00:27:14,409 --> 00:27:17,049
The commission had written to the court
on the first of July,

779
00:27:17,109 --> 00:27:18,708
asking that the appeals be held

780
00:27:18,709 --> 00:27:21,349
until it had deliberated on its findings,

781
00:27:21,409 --> 00:27:23,938
which it expected to do the following June.

782
00:27:23,997 --> 00:27:25,097
Read that again,

783
00:27:25,157 --> 00:27:27,036
because it is the strangest sentence

784
00:27:27,037 --> 00:27:28,370
in this story.

785
00:27:28,430 --> 00:27:30,949
A criminal appeal about a hundred

786
00:27:30,950 --> 00:27:34,129
and fifty-nine deaths was paused, by the court,

787
00:27:34,130 --> 00:27:36,067
because nobody had yet established what happened.

788
00:27:36,068 --> 00:27:38,769
Nearly three years after the night itself.

789
00:27:38,829 --> 00:27:40,188
The commission is still working,

790
00:27:40,189 --> 00:27:43,202
and it is the reason this story is not over.

791
00:27:43,262 --> 00:27:46,182
In January 2024 the President at the time,

792
00:27:46,242 --> 00:27:47,342
Yoon Suk Yeol,

793
00:27:47,402 --> 00:27:49,441
rejected a special act to investigate

794
00:27:49,442 --> 00:27:51,801
the disaster, the government arguing

795
00:27:51,802 --> 00:27:54,321
that an opposition-driven committee undermined

796
00:27:54,322 --> 00:27:56,227
constitutional principles.

797
00:27:56,287 --> 00:27:59,847
A commission was established in September 2024,

798
00:27:59,907 --> 00:28:02,587
with a name that is itself a sentence:

799
00:28:02,647 --> 00:28:04,646
the National Commission for the Investigation

800
00:28:04,647 --> 00:28:08,286
of the October 29 Itaewon Disaster and Prevention

801
00:28:08,287 --> 00:28:09,669
of Recurrence.

802
00:28:09,729 --> 00:28:13,789
In July 2025 a new President, Lee Jae Myung,

803
00:28:13,849 --> 00:28:16,108
ordered
the setting up of a further investigation team

804
00:28:16,109 --> 00:28:19,536
of police and prosecutors, to work alongside it.

805
00:28:19,596 --> 00:28:20,997
He apologised.

806
00:28:21,057 --> 00:28:23,057
As the head of the state, he said,

807
00:28:23,077 --> 00:28:25,236
I would like to formally apologize on behalf

808
00:28:25,237 --> 00:28:26,496
of the government for failing

809
00:28:26,497 --> 00:28:29,276
to fulfill its responsibility to protect the lives

810
00:28:29,277 --> 00:28:30,957
and safety of the people.

811
00:28:31,017 --> 00:28:32,377
At the same time,

812
00:28:32,437 --> 00:28:34,776
a lawyer representing the victims' families,

813
00:28:34,777 --> 00:28:37,816
Song Hae-jin, said police records and information

814
00:28:37,817 --> 00:28:39,876
about the government's response had been withheld

815
00:28:39,877 --> 00:28:41,242
from the commission.

816
00:28:41,302 --> 00:28:43,801
At the hearing you heard about a few minutes ago,

817
00:28:43,802 --> 00:28:44,881
a survivor testified

818
00:28:44,882 --> 00:28:47,208
and police officials traded blame.

819
00:28:47,268 --> 00:28:48,708
Kim Kwang-ho —

820
00:28:48,768 --> 00:28:50,107
the former Seoul police chief,

821
00:28:50,108 --> 00:28:53,708
acquitted at first instance in October 2024 —

822
00:28:53,768 --> 00:28:55,694
refused to take the witness oath.

823
00:28:55,695 --> 00:28:57,834
In May it asked prosecutors to investigate

824
00:28:57,835 --> 00:28:59,795
the district office chief again,

825
00:28:59,855 --> 00:29:01,494
and a former Itaewon station chief

826
00:29:01,495 --> 00:29:02,894
over an allegation of perjury

827
00:29:02,895 --> 00:29:04,944
at a parliamentary hearing.

828
00:29:05,004 --> 00:29:06,203
And in June it concluded

829
00:29:06,204 --> 00:29:07,983
that it needed another year and three months,

830
00:29:07,984 --> 00:29:09,443
to December 2027,

831
00:29:09,444 --> 00:29:11,143
and said it would be looking upward —

832
00:29:11,144 --> 00:29:13,023
at the chain of command,

833
00:29:13,024 --> 00:29:15,414
including the Office of the President.

834
00:29:15,474 --> 00:29:17,993
Four years on, the question of who was responsible

835
00:29:17,994 --> 00:29:19,954
for that street is still open,

836
00:29:20,014 --> 00:29:24,041
and it is being asked higher up than it was.

837
00:29:24,101 --> 00:29:27,200
Go to Itaewon now, on the last weekend in October,

838
00:29:27,201 --> 00:29:30,518
and you will find that something has changed.

839
00:29:30,578 --> 00:29:32,697
There is a temporary median barrier down

840
00:29:32,698 --> 00:29:34,317
the middle of World Food Street,

841
00:29:34,318 --> 00:29:36,948
put there to make people walk one way.

842
00:29:37,008 --> 00:29:39,047
Officers and station staff guide people

843
00:29:39,048 --> 00:29:41,799
through the underground station
to stop it backing up.

844
00:29:41,859 --> 00:29:44,800
A mobile patrol unit starts at six in the evening.

845
00:29:44,853 --> 00:29:46,372
Streets are checked for hazards,

846
00:29:46,373 --> 00:29:47,832
and somebody makes sure the cameras

847
00:29:47,833 --> 00:29:50,062
and the emergency bells work.

848
00:29:50,122 --> 00:29:51,541
When the road gets crowded,

849
00:29:51,542 --> 00:29:53,427
traffic police blow whistles.

850
00:29:53,487 --> 00:29:55,074
And there are signs.

851
00:29:55,134 --> 00:29:57,593
The Korea JoongAng Daily quoted one of them:

852
00:29:57,594 --> 00:29:59,786
crowded areas can be dangerous.

853
00:29:59,846 --> 00:30:02,226
Above all of that there is now a system,

854
00:30:02,286 --> 00:30:04,925
and the Seoul Metropolitan Government describes it

855
00:30:04,926 --> 00:30:05,825
in its own words

856
00:30:05,826 --> 00:30:08,806
as an intelligent people counting system,

857
00:30:08,866 --> 00:30:11,345
which automatically monitors crowding

858
00:30:11,346 --> 00:30:13,685
and raises alarms if it detects signs

859
00:30:13,686 --> 00:30:15,458
of dangerous crowd problems.

860
00:30:15,518 --> 00:30:16,417
Cameras connected

861
00:30:16,418 --> 00:30:19,097
to analytical software automatically calculate

862
00:30:19,098 --> 00:30:21,137
the number of people per unit area,

863
00:30:21,138 --> 00:30:22,717
and when they see something,

864
00:30:22,718 --> 00:30:25,538
they tell the local disaster situation rooms,

865
00:30:25,598 --> 00:30:26,878
the city government,

866
00:30:26,938 --> 00:30:28,837
the fire and disaster headquarters,

867
00:30:28,838 --> 00:30:30,247
and the police.

868
00:30:30,307 --> 00:30:32,566
The city listed seventy-one areas where large

869
00:30:32,567 --> 00:30:33,506
crowds were expected,

870
00:30:33,507 --> 00:30:37,188
and put nine hundred and nine cameras into them.

871
00:30:37,248 --> 00:30:39,267
The page does not say at what density

872
00:30:39,268 --> 00:30:40,527
the alarm goes off,

873
00:30:40,528 --> 00:30:43,267
and this film is not going to invent a number

874
00:30:43,268 --> 00:30:44,268
for it.

875
00:30:44,328 --> 00:30:46,567
Nine hundred and nine cameras,

876
00:30:46,568 --> 00:30:48,249
and a plastic barrier at knee height.

877
00:30:48,250 --> 00:30:50,440
That is the part worth sitting with.

878
00:30:50,500 --> 00:30:52,819
What was missing in that street was not technology

879
00:30:52,820 --> 00:30:54,827
and it was not money.

880
00:30:54,887 --> 00:30:56,426
It was a barrier, a direction,

881
00:30:56,427 --> 00:30:58,766
and somebody whose job it was to decide

882
00:30:58,767 --> 00:31:01,223
those two things before the evening started.

883
00:31:01,224 --> 00:31:02,857
You go into crowds.

884
00:31:02,917 --> 00:31:04,337
Everybody does —

885
00:31:04,397 --> 00:31:07,237
a station at rush hour, a stadium emptying,

886
00:31:07,297 --> 00:31:08,776
a street at New Year.

887
00:31:08,836 --> 00:31:10,235
The next time you are in one

888
00:31:10,236 --> 00:31:11,815
and it stops feeling like a crowd

889
00:31:11,816 --> 00:31:13,815
and starts feeling like a current,

890
00:31:13,816 --> 00:31:15,975
the useful question is not whether somebody

891
00:31:15,976 --> 00:31:17,249
is watching.

892
00:31:17,309 --> 00:31:20,382
It is whether anybody has been given the job.

893
00:31:20,442 --> 00:31:21,981
Somewhere there is a street you walk

894
00:31:21,982 --> 00:31:23,561
through without thinking.

895
00:31:23,621 --> 00:31:26,361
Ask who decided that it was safe.
